@startuml sd05_tick
!include ../style.iuml
autonumber

participant "Central Harness\n(shared clock)" as H
participant "CTC Office" as CTC
participant "Track Model" as TM
box "Host PC — Track Ctrl HW process" #F7F9FC
participant "HarnessEndpoint" as EP <<planned>>
participant "RemoteTrackController\n+ PiSerialLink" as Remote <<planned>>
participant "TrackControllerState" as State
end box
box "Raspberry Pi 5" #F2F5F9
participant "PiLinkServer" as Pi <<planned>>
participant "HwTrackController" as Ctrl
participant "Wayside ×N" as W
end box

note over H
  Tick k. The harness maps tick k−1's CTC Office and
  Track Model outputs into this module's inputs (D005).
end note
H -> H : map CTC suggestions (per train) to\nper-block Suggestion; drop train IDs;\nmap closures, switch commands, occupancy,\nswitch / crossing / signal read-back
H -> EP : {"id", "tick": k, "op": "step", "dt": 0.1, "time_s", inputs}
EP -> Remote : step(dt, inputs)
Remote -> Pi : same request, newline JSON over USB (D027)
Pi -> Ctrl : step(dt, inputs)
Ctrl -> Ctrl : validate dt and every input\n(reject before any state changes)
alt invalid
  Ctrl --> Pi : InvalidInputError / InvalidTimeStepError
  Pi --> Remote : error reply
  Remote --> EP : raise
  EP --> H : {"id", "tick": k, "error"}
  H -> H : show and log the rejected tick
else valid
  Ctrl -> Ctrl : stall = first wayside not ready, if any
  loop every wayside of the line
    Ctrl -> W : scan(dt, time_s, ctc, track_model, stall)
    ref over W : SD-06 Scan cycle
    W --> Ctrl : WaysideScan (commands + CtcReport)
  end
  Ctrl --> Pi : TrackControllerOutputs
  Pi --> Remote : {"id", "ok": outputs}
  Remote --> EP : outputs
  EP --> H : {"id", "tick": k, outputs}
end
EP ->> State : ticks advanced (window refreshes within 100 ms)
H -> TM : (tick k+1) track circuits, switch, signal\nand crossing commands
H -> CTC : (tick k+1) per-wayside reports:\noccupancy, states, ready per line
note over H, Pi
  At 10x the harness sends 100 ticks per real second and waits for every reply,
  so the USB round trip and the scan together must stay under 10 ms (D017).
end note
@enduml
